# Changelog
All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

## [Unreleased]
- `ManagedClientTokenIntrospectResponse` has `applicationId` and `BackboneOpaqueTokenIntrospector` puts it in the principal as the `application_id` claim, so a resource server can limit a managed client to its own application. `null` against a backbone-rest that does not return it yet.
- Upgrade stack to Java 25, Spring Boot 4.1.1 and Spring Cloud 2025.1.3.
- Security: override Jackson (2.22.3 / 3.2.3), Netty (4.2.18.Final), Logback (1.6.5) and BouncyCastle (1.86) to fix reported CVEs.
- Rename project to UMDC Security OAuth (`com.umdc` group and packages).
- Dependencies: Spring Boot 4.1.2, Spring Cloud 2025.1.4 / OpenFeign 5.0.4, Tomcat 11.0.27, Jackson 2.22.4 / 3.2.4, Netty 4.2.20.Final, Logback 1.6.6, Gson 2.15.0, Commons Lang 3.21.0, Mockito 5.24.0, ASM 9.11.1, JaCoCo 0.8.16, Surefire 3.6.1, Compiler plugin 3.16.0, Resources plugin 3.5.0 and JXR 3.6.0.
- Security (Snyk): pin Hibernate Validator 9.1.6.Final and Objenesis 3.6 in `dependencyManagement`; Tomcat and Jackson 3 bumped to patched releases.
- Jackson 3 migration: remove `jjwt-jackson` (Jackson 2) and add `Jackson3JwtSerializer` / `Jackson3JwtDeserializer` (`com.umdc.security.jwt.json`), registered via `META-INF/services` so JJWT uses `tools.jackson` for JSON. Duplicate keys and trailing tokens are still rejected.
- Remaining Jackson 2 artifacts (`jackson-databind`, `-dataformat-yaml`, `-datatype-jsr310`) come transitively from `swagger-core` (through `commons-services`) and are pinned to 2.22.4.
- Tests: add unit tests for the Jackson 3 adapters, service defaults, controller, configuration beans and properties (139 tests, method coverage 88.5%).
- Docs: add user guide and technical guide under `docs/`.

## Version 0.0.1
- Initial version.
- Security OAuth library added.
- Spring Boot (3.3.5) and Spring Cloud dependencies (4.1.3 / 2023.0.3) included.
- Spring Security and Keycloak integrated for authentication.
- Add JWT token for secured API access.
- default application properties Included.
- Updated to receive multiple parameters to include in the JWT token.
